== CANON-20 / ADR-0008: `..` (level 10) binds weaker than `+` (level 5), so
== `X in 1..N + 1` means `X in (1..(N + 1))`. The test is shape-discriminating:
== the wrong grouping `(X in 1..N) + 1` would add an Integer to a Bool and
== fail semantic analysis.
Module PrecedenceInRangeAdditive

Main :
    N Integer := 3
    X Integer := 4
    B Bool := X in 1..N + 1
    PutLn(B)
;
